    card title "Numbers to 100"

A: How much is a coffee in Masha's café?
    draw o_coffee o_q

A: To understand her answer, you'll need numbers past ten, all the way to a hundred.
    draw o_range

    erase o_coffee o_q o_range

B: Оди́ннадцать.
    draw a_11

A: It's three pieces glued together: оди́н, one; на, on; and дцать, said tsat, a worn-down де́сять, ten.
    draw p_one g_one p_na g_na p_ten g_ten

A: One on ten: that's eleven.
    draw a_word

    erase pageA

B: Оди́ннадцать, двена́дцать, трина́дцать, четы́рнадцать, пятна́дцать.
    draw d11 w11 d12 w12 d13 w13 d14 w14 d15 w15 parallel true

A: Two on ten, three on ten, four, five: every teen is the digit, then на, then дцать.
    highlight w12 w13 w14 w15 part на color #f2c14e

B: Шестна́дцать, семна́дцать, восемна́дцать, девятна́дцать.
    draw d16 w16 d17 w17 d18 w18 d19 w19 parallel true

A: Three spellings to watch. Twelve starts with две, not два.
    highlight w12 part ^две color #d0865f

A: Fourteen drops the е of четы́ре: четы́рнадцать.
    highlight w14 part ^четыр color #d0865f

B: And the soft sign drops out: пять, but пятна́дцать; семь, but семна́дцать.
    highlight w15 w16 w17 w18 w19 effect underline color #8f887c

A: The tens drop the на: два́дцать is simply two tens, and три́дцать, three tens.
    draw d20 w20 d30 w30

A: So listen for the stress. Трина́дцать, three on ten, is stressed on на: thirteen. Три́дцать, three tens, is stressed on три: thirty.
    highlight w13 w30

    hide bdigits

    ask "Which one is thirty? Tap it." choose ["w12","w13","w14","w15","w18","w19","w20","w30"] answer w30 voice a
        intro: The digits are gone: can you still read the cards?
        right: Три́дцать: three tens, with no на in the middle.
        wrong: Thirty has no на: look for три right before дцать.

    show bdigits

    hide board

    draw r_d20 r_w20 r_d30 r_w30 parallel true

A: Forty breaks the pattern: со́рок is a word all of its own.
    draw r_d40 r_w40

B: Пятьдеся́т: пять and деся́т, five tens, stressed at the end.
    draw r_d50 r_w50

A: Here пять keeps its soft sign, and ten loses its own.
    highlight r_w50 part ^пять color #d0865f

A: And a hundred is short and easy: сто.
    draw r_d100 r_w100

B: Шестьдеся́т, се́мьдесят, во́семьдесят: sixty, seventy and eighty are built like пятьдеся́т.
    draw r_d60 r_w60 r_d70 r_w70 r_d80 r_w80

A: But ninety is девяно́сто, a word of its own, like со́рок.
    draw r_d90 r_w90

A: Anything in between is tens, then units, with no and: два́дцать пять is twenty-five.
    draw c_25 c_25w

    hide tensrow

A: Now back to Masha's café: there's a menu with prices, and I ask the question every visitor needs.
    draw tom tom_name masha masha_name menu m_coffee m_tea

    dialogue talk speakers.a tom speakers.b masha turns [{"by":"a","text":"Ско́лько сто́ит ко́фе?","gloss":"How much is the coffee?"},{"by":"b","text":"Сто рубле́й.","gloss":"A hundred roubles."},{"by":"a","text":"А чай?","gloss":"And the tea?"},{"by":"b","text":"Пятьдеся́т рубле́й.","gloss":"Fifty roubles."}] size 1.4

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

A: Ско́лько сто́ит means how much does it cost: put any thing on the menu after it.
    highlight talk_1_words part "Ско́лько сто́ит" color #c9871a

B: The number comes first, then рубле́й, roubles: that's its form after five to twenty, and after any number ending in nought or five to nine.
    highlight talk_4_words part рубле́й color #c9871a

A: After a number ending in one to four, like два́дцать оди́н, it changes, but that's for a later lesson.
    highlight m_coffee m_tea effect underline color #8f887c

    erase talk menugrp

    hide speakers

    cards match size 1.8 y 440
        * "двена́дцать" match "12"
        * "пятна́дцать" match "15"
        * "со́рок" match "40"
        * "пятьдеся́т" match "50"

    ask "Match each Russian number to its digits." on match store m stage own voice a test t1
        intro: Five questions now, from memory, then your score.
        right: Двена́дцать, twelve; пятна́дцать, fifteen; со́рок, forty; and пятьдеся́т, fifty.
        wrong: You got {m} on the first try.

    erase match

    quiz "Which one is 13? Pick one." store q2 reveal.text "13 = трина́дцать" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 380 reveal.style label reveal.size 72 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Three on ten: на in the middle makes it a teen.
        wrong: Thirteen is three ON ten: look for на.
        + трина́дцать
        * три́дцать
        * три

    erase q2_stamp

    ask "Молоко́ — три́дцать пять рубле́й. How much is the milk? Type it in digits." answer ["35"] store q3 default "35" reveal.text "молоко́: 35" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 380 reveal.style label reveal.size 90 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Thirty-five: три́дцать, three tens, then пять.
        wrong: Three tens, then five.

    erase q3_stamp

    ask "Type forty in Russian." answer ["сорок"] store q4 default сорок reveal.text "40 = со́рок" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 380 reveal.style label reveal.size 80 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: Со́рок: forty is the one with a word all of its own.
        wrong: Forty breaks the pattern: it has no дцать at all.

    erase q4_stamp

    ask "Type twenty-five in Russian." answer ["двадцать пять","двадцатьпять"] store q5 default "двадцать пять" reveal.text "25 = два́дцать пять" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 380 reveal.style label reveal.size 72 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: Два́дцать пять: the tens, then the units, with no and.
        wrong: Twenty, then five, as two words.

    erase q5_stamp

    show tensrow

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

A: So the teens are a digit on ten, most tens count tens, (@highlight r_w40 r_w90 r_w100@) со́рок, девяно́сто and сто stand alone, and a price takes рубле́й.

    hide tensrow

B: Ко́фе? Сто рубле́й! Next time: how to ask who, what and when. Пока́!
    icon e_coffee size 150 set twemoji x 330 y 150 or ["coffee"] icon_look picture of "hot beverage"
    text e_price "сто рубле́й" #3d3833 say "Сто рубле́й!" say_voice b x 620 y 150 font_size 64

